      </article></section><div class="essay-library"><section class="essay-group" aria-labelledby="mathematics-essays"><h2 id="mathematics-essays" class="essay-group-label">Proof and explanation</h2><p class="essay-group-description">Constructions, comparisons, and the difference between settling a theorem and making it usable.</p><p class="essay-feature-reference"><a href="#featured-continuity-essay">Continuity as Organized Discrete Data</a> is featured above.</p><article class="essay-card"><p class="meta">Proof and understanding · 11 min read · <time datetime="2026-10-08">October 8, 2026</time> · Revised <time datetime="2026-11-09">November 9, 2026</time></p><h3><a href="/essays/what-a-new-proof-makes-possible">What a New Proof Makes Possible</a></h3><p class="essay-subtitle">Old theorems and the changing means of understanding</p><p>How new proofs of familiar theorems expose mechanisms, improve estimates, and connect mathematical subjects. Comparing the arguments reveals why their constructions work, where they generalize, and what further questions they open.</p><div class="text-links essay-index-actions" data-essay-downloads="what-a-new-proof-makes-possible"><a href="/essays/what-a-new-proof-makes-possible">Read the essay</a><a href="/assets/essays/what-a-new-proof-makes-possible.9b19b4a9be61834e.pdf" aria-label="Download PDF of What a New Proof Makes Possible">PDF</a><a href="/assets/essays/what-a-new-proof-makes-possible.31e317ae22720c4a.md" aria-label="Download text of What a New Proof Makes Possible (.md)">Text (.md)</a></div></article><article class="essay-card"><p class="meta">Mathematics and intellectual life · 6 min read · <time datetime="2026-10-17">October 17, 2026</time> · Revised <time datetime="2026-11-09">November 9, 2026</time></p><h3><a href="/essays/when-a-description-becomes-a-verdict">When a Description Becomes a Verdict</a></h3><p class="essay-subtitle">Expertise, explanation, and the scope of judgment</p><p>How to test whether a description